cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use jspassgen-lsp in research or production write-ups, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "jspassgen-lsp: a language server for weak literal secrets"
abstract: >-
  The language server of the jspassgen suite. It is planned to report
  weak or low-entropy literal secrets in configuration and .env files,
  with a code action that replaces one with a value generated locally by
  jspassgen. The current version completes the LSP handshake only.
authors:
  - family-names: Rousseau
    given-names: Sebastien
version: "0.0.24"
date-released: "2026-11-20"
# Dual-licensed, at the user's option (LICENSE-APACHE, LICENSE-MIT).
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/sebastienrousseau/jspassgen-lsp"
keywords:
  - language-server
  - lsp
  - password
  - secrets
  - dotenv
  - entropy
  - JavaScript
